1
00:00:06,132 --> 00:00:08,551
<i>Is it too much to ask for a single reply?</i>

2
00:00:08,634 --> 00:00:10,761
Have some consideration, Ben!

3
00:00:10,845 --> 00:00:12,972
<i>I'm sorry.</i>
<i>It's my fault that I didn't call you.</i>

4
00:00:13,055 --> 00:00:14,890
<i>I'm really, really sorry.</i>

5
00:00:14,974 --> 00:00:18,185
There are plenty of women
who want your husband.

6
00:00:18,269 --> 00:00:23,441
<i>He's handsome,</i>
<i>kind, smart, rich--</i>

7
00:00:23,524 --> 00:00:25,067
So do I just do nothing?

8
00:00:25,151 --> 00:00:26,318
Of course not!

9
00:00:26,402 --> 00:00:29,405
<i>I am Benjamin Santos's wife.</i>

10
00:00:29,488 --> 00:00:31,157
<i>Benjamin...</i>

11
00:00:31,240 --> 00:00:33,367
Come on! I know you know him.

12
00:00:33,451 --> 00:00:34,952
You're his mistress, aren't you?

13
00:00:35,035 --> 00:00:36,537
<i>Are you calling my husband?</i>

14
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:38,539
<i>No, I'm calling the village patrol</i>

15
00:00:38,622 --> 00:00:40,916
<i>if you don't stop with your accusations!</i>

16
00:00:51,719 --> 00:00:52,720
Come in.

17
00:00:53,679 --> 00:00:55,347
Stay here for now, Caloy.

18
00:00:56,348 --> 00:00:59,101
Mama will be right back, okay?

19
00:00:59,185 --> 00:01:01,604
I just have to talk to Auntie Beth.

20
00:01:03,522 --> 00:01:07,443
Diane, let me remind you,
maybe this time it'll sink in.

21
00:01:07,526 --> 00:01:09,361
You're an idiot, and you've lost it.

22
00:01:10,154 --> 00:01:12,031
What the hell are you planning to do?

23
00:01:13,282 --> 00:01:15,034
I don't know, Beth!

24
00:01:15,618 --> 00:01:17,244
What do you mean you don't know?

25
00:01:18,621 --> 00:01:20,873
How long are you staying here?

26
00:01:21,707 --> 00:01:23,042
Come on, Beth.

27
00:01:23,125 --> 00:01:24,543
Calm down, okay?

28
00:01:24,627 --> 00:01:27,087
I need some time to think.

29
00:01:27,171 --> 00:01:28,005
What? No.

30
00:01:28,088 --> 00:01:30,049
You need to decide now.

31
00:01:30,132 --> 00:01:31,258
This is unbelievable.

32
00:01:31,342 --> 00:01:32,760
You know how crazy your ex is.

33
00:01:32,843 --> 00:01:34,261
Screw that guy!

34
00:01:34,345 --> 00:01:36,514
He can't keep my son away from me!

35
00:01:36,597 --> 00:01:38,808
He hasn't seen
half of what I'm capable of yet.

36
00:01:38,891 --> 00:01:41,644
And even if he finds us here,
I won't give him Caloy.

37
00:01:46,148 --> 00:01:47,149
Wait, Beth!

38
00:01:47,233 --> 00:01:48,651
Calm down.

39
00:01:50,319 --> 00:01:51,403
Who is it?

40
00:01:51,487 --> 00:01:52,488
Beth.

41
00:01:53,405 --> 00:01:54,907
There's a delivery downstairs.

42
00:01:54,990 --> 00:01:56,450
It might be yours.

43
00:01:56,534 --> 00:01:59,203
Oh, all right, thank you.
I'll check it out.

44
00:02:02,164 --> 00:02:04,333
- It's already paid for, right?
- Yes, ma'am.

45
00:02:12,591 --> 00:02:13,843
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

46
00:02:31,861 --> 00:02:32,862
Hello?

47
00:02:34,029 --> 00:02:35,948
Ben, Ana was here!

48
00:02:36,532 --> 00:02:37,867
What?

49
00:02:37,950 --> 00:02:40,578
<i>She was pulling up when I got downstairs.</i>

50
00:02:41,370 --> 00:02:42,454
What did she say?

51
00:02:42,538 --> 00:02:44,164
She was asking questions.

52
00:02:44,248 --> 00:02:46,166
I didn't say anything.

53
00:02:46,250 --> 00:02:47,918
I lied.

54
00:02:48,002 --> 00:02:49,503
<i>What about Regina?</i>

55
00:02:49,587 --> 00:02:51,005
Ana didn't see her.

56
00:02:51,964 --> 00:02:53,465
Good thing Regina was quiet.

57
00:02:54,216 --> 00:02:55,718
Okay, good.

58
00:02:56,218 --> 00:02:57,303
<i>Ben.</i>

59
00:02:57,970 --> 00:03:01,140
Her coming here means she knows something.

60
00:03:04,852 --> 00:03:07,688
I'll find a way to throw her off.

61
00:03:07,771 --> 00:03:11,400
It's too late. She knows where we are.

62
00:03:11,483 --> 00:03:13,777
How long are you going to hide us here?

63
00:03:18,532 --> 00:03:20,618
I'll figure something out.

64
00:03:22,119 --> 00:03:23,537
I'll take care of this.

65
00:03:49,355 --> 00:03:50,189
So, what now?

66
00:03:50,272 --> 00:03:52,066
I don't know.
J-Just drive!

67
00:03:52,149 --> 00:03:54,068
- Just keep driving!
- Okay, okay, okay, okay!

68
00:04:45,536 --> 00:04:47,329
Are you sure about this?

69
00:04:48,455 --> 00:04:49,623
No.

70
00:04:51,542 --> 00:04:52,626
I'll stay.

71
00:04:53,711 --> 00:04:54,712
No, it's okay, Kat.

72
00:04:54,795 --> 00:04:56,463
I need some time alone.

73
00:04:57,256 --> 00:04:58,674
Eat something.

74
00:04:58,757 --> 00:05:00,676
Order room service.

75
00:05:03,470 --> 00:05:07,224
Don't worry, it's not Ben.
It's my driver. He's almost here.

76
00:05:11,228 --> 00:05:12,646
Attorney Ben?

77
00:05:13,188 --> 00:05:14,690
Yes, I think it was him.

78
00:05:14,773 --> 00:05:17,192
I think it was his car that I saw pass by.

79
00:05:18,610 --> 00:05:20,362
And why would he pass by here?

80
00:05:20,446 --> 00:05:22,364
Does he still have sessions with you?

81
00:05:23,449 --> 00:05:24,783
He does.

82
00:05:27,995 --> 00:05:30,330
Diane, he cannot see you here.

83
00:05:30,414 --> 00:05:31,707
Well, he didn't.

84
00:05:32,541 --> 00:05:35,377
For now.
But you could cross paths in the future.

85
00:05:37,629 --> 00:05:40,215
He won't be happy if he finds out

86
00:05:40,299 --> 00:05:41,467
that we know each other.

87
00:05:41,550 --> 00:05:43,635
And so what?

88
00:05:43,719 --> 00:05:46,680
He doesn't know
I did a loyalty test on him, right?

89
00:05:47,306 --> 00:05:48,557
Ben's very smart.

90
00:05:49,641 --> 00:05:51,310
And you're being paranoid.

91
00:05:51,393 --> 00:05:53,854
Diane, you don't understand.

92
00:05:55,773 --> 00:05:58,275
You're making things
too complicated, Beth.

93
00:05:58,358 --> 00:06:00,319
You shouldn't even be involved
in his life anymore.

94
00:06:00,402 --> 00:06:02,488
Your loyalty test is over.

95
00:06:02,571 --> 00:06:06,325
But our physical therapy sessions
aren't over, Diane.

96
00:06:07,576 --> 00:06:09,411
And we've become friends.

97
00:06:10,370 --> 00:06:11,872
This is different.

98
00:06:12,790 --> 00:06:14,458
Just don't leave the apartment.

99
00:06:14,541 --> 00:06:15,709
What?

100
00:06:16,835 --> 00:06:18,003
Seriously, Beth?

101
00:06:18,754 --> 00:06:21,423
Okay, fine.
You can go out when we have a session.

102
00:06:21,840 --> 00:06:23,759
So I can make sure he won't see you.

103
00:06:24,510 --> 00:06:25,594
That's what we'll do.

104
00:06:26,220 --> 00:06:29,389
Seriously, Beth. You're overthinking this.

105
00:06:33,143 --> 00:06:35,229
No matter what happens,

106
00:06:35,312 --> 00:06:37,815
I hope you get through this.

107
00:06:38,899 --> 00:06:40,067
I will.

108
00:06:41,026 --> 00:06:42,069
Go on.

109
00:06:52,329 --> 00:06:54,748


110
00:07:01,255 --> 00:07:02,589


111
00:07:05,884 --> 00:07:08,387
All right. Let's eat, Ging.

112
00:07:10,931 --> 00:07:12,766
There you go. Dig in.

113
00:07:13,559 --> 00:07:15,727
- We're not leaving!

114
00:07:15,811 --> 00:07:17,396
We're not going anywhere!

115
00:07:18,647 --> 00:07:19,648
Regina, calm down.

116
00:07:19,731 --> 00:07:21,191
I heard you on the phone with Ben.

117
00:07:21,692 --> 00:07:23,110
It was nothing.

118
00:07:23,193 --> 00:07:24,778
We are not going anywhere, understood?

119
00:07:24,862 --> 00:07:27,614
We are not leaving
because Joel's coming back for me here!

120
00:07:27,698 --> 00:07:30,200
- Give that to me.
If you force me, I will run away!

121
00:07:30,284 --> 00:07:31,702
We are not leaving, Regina!

122
00:07:31,785 --> 00:07:33,453
Give me the knife. Let go!

123
00:07:33,537 --> 00:07:35,664
Drop it! Drop the knife!

124
00:07:35,747 --> 00:07:37,499
We're not going anywhere.

125
00:07:38,208 --> 00:07:39,877
Who said we're leaving?

126
00:07:40,460 --> 00:07:41,712
That's not happening.

127
00:07:42,337 --> 00:07:43,839
So we're not leaving?

128
00:07:44,590 --> 00:07:47,176
- No.
Really?

129
00:07:48,552 --> 00:07:49,636
Yes, Regina.

130
00:07:53,056 --> 00:07:54,391
What a mess.

131
00:08:00,272 --> 00:08:01,607


132
00:08:10,574 --> 00:08:11,742


133
00:08:11,825 --> 00:08:14,244


134
00:08:16,705 --> 00:08:18,373
<i>Someone from here</i>
<i>has been calling him.</i>

135
00:08:18,457 --> 00:08:20,000
<i>If you're the only one who lives here,</i>

136
00:08:20,083 --> 00:08:22,002
<i>then you're the one</i>
<i>who's been calling him!</i>

137
00:08:22,419 --> 00:08:24,838
<i>Like I said,</i>
<i>you have the wrong house.</i>

138
00:08:24,922 --> 00:08:26,882
<i>No one named Benjamin lives here.</i>

139
00:08:26,965 --> 00:08:28,300
Yes, miss?

140
00:08:28,383 --> 00:08:29,551
How may I help you?

141
00:08:35,849 --> 00:08:37,434
<i>Where are you?</i>

142
00:08:39,811 --> 00:08:41,396
<i>I'll pick you up.</i>

143
00:09:03,001 --> 00:09:06,171


144
00:09:08,465 --> 00:09:11,718


145
00:09:53,760 --> 00:09:56,096
It's scorching!

146
00:09:56,722 --> 00:09:57,556


147
00:10:00,392 --> 00:10:02,144
God, it's so hot!

148
00:10:02,227 --> 00:10:03,395
Hi, ma'am. Here's your order.

149
00:10:03,478 --> 00:10:04,730
- Sorry to keep you waiting.
Miss? Miss?

150
00:10:04,813 --> 00:10:06,481
- Yes?
Four gin and tonics, please.

151
00:10:06,565 --> 00:10:08,317
- Okay. Let me just get that...
Oh, and two whiskey sours.

152
00:10:08,400 --> 00:10:09,318
Wait, wait, wait.

153
00:10:09,401 --> 00:10:11,153
Can you make that
five gin and tonics, please?

154
00:10:11,236 --> 00:10:12,988
And then three mojitos
with less sugar, please.

155
00:10:13,071 --> 00:10:15,782
Oh, can I add more margarita,
please, without ice?

156
00:10:15,866 --> 00:10:18,076
And then follow up on the tequila.
Thank you!

157
00:10:18,452 --> 00:10:21,913
Okay, so that's
five gin and tonics, and one mojito,

158
00:10:21,997 --> 00:10:25,459
and one margarita without ice,
and... sorry?

159
00:10:25,542 --> 00:10:26,585
Three mojitos, less sugar.

160
00:10:26,668 --> 00:10:28,086
Three mojitos, less sugar. Okay. Got that.

161
00:10:28,170 --> 00:10:29,713
- Okay, thank you.
Thank you!

162
00:10:29,796 --> 00:10:31,381
- Excuse me.
Yes?

163
00:10:31,465 --> 00:10:33,091
Where is my order?
Two whiskeys on the rocks.

164
00:10:33,175 --> 00:10:34,718
Two whiskeys on the rocks. Got that, sir.

165
00:10:34,801 --> 00:10:36,303
- Excuse me. Can you clean this up, please?
Yes?

166
00:10:41,475 --> 00:10:43,060
Sorry. I'm so, so sorry.

167
00:10:43,143 --> 00:10:44,728
I'm really sorry.

168
00:10:44,811 --> 00:10:45,812
Um...

169
00:10:47,147 --> 00:10:49,983

I'll just get you a complimentary drink.

170
00:10:50,067 --> 00:10:52,861
This is for table 4.

171
00:10:52,944 --> 00:10:53,987
For clearing.

172
00:10:54,071 --> 00:10:56,281
- Table 12 placed an order.
What is it?

173
00:10:57,324 --> 00:10:58,700
Uh...

174
00:10:59,618 --> 00:11:00,952
It's...

175
00:11:01,036 --> 00:11:03,580
four gin and tonics, three mojitos,

176
00:11:03,663 --> 00:11:05,499
and one margarita, no sugar.

177
00:11:05,582 --> 00:11:07,084
Huh? One more time.

178
00:11:07,167 --> 00:11:08,877
It's five gin and tonics,
three mojitos,

179
00:11:08,960 --> 00:11:10,379
and one margarita with no sugar.

180
00:11:10,462 --> 00:11:11,630
- Got it?
- Got it.

181
00:11:13,465 --> 00:11:15,050
Hi, sir. Sorry to keep you waiting.

182
00:11:24,851 --> 00:11:25,936
Hello?

183
00:11:27,479 --> 00:11:28,480
Ah, yes.

184
00:11:28,563 --> 00:11:32,067
Is this the security
department of Saguil <i>azucarera?</i>

185
00:11:32,150 --> 00:11:35,070
This is Ana, Attorney Ben's wife.

186
00:11:35,153 --> 00:11:36,488
I just want to ask,

187
00:11:36,571 --> 00:11:40,325
has anyone claimed the cell phone
Attorney Ben left behind?

188
00:11:42,619 --> 00:11:44,287
<i> Yes, ma'am.</i>

189
00:11:45,247 --> 00:11:46,331
Really?

190
00:11:47,082 --> 00:11:48,166
Who?

191
00:11:48,708 --> 00:11:53,338
<i>I didn't catch their name,</i>
<i>but they're not from here.</i>

192
00:11:53,880 --> 00:11:55,173
Not a local?

193
00:11:56,133 --> 00:11:58,552
From the neighboring town?

194
00:11:58,635 --> 00:11:59,970
<i>I believe so.</i>

195
00:12:02,806 --> 00:12:05,892
Do you remember what they look like?

196
00:12:07,644 --> 00:12:08,728
Uh...

197
00:12:11,022 --> 00:12:12,190
Is she pretty?

198
00:12:13,817 --> 00:12:14,985
Sexy?

199
00:12:17,279 --> 00:12:20,365
<i>Ma'am, the phone was claimed by a man.</i>

200
00:12:22,409 --> 00:12:23,493
A man?

201
00:12:28,248 --> 00:12:30,000
Uh, okay.

202
00:12:30,083 --> 00:12:31,334
Okay, okay.

203
00:12:31,418 --> 00:12:32,419
<i>Yes, ma'am.</i>

204
00:12:32,502 --> 00:12:34,463
<i>He said he dropped his phone</i>

205
00:12:34,546 --> 00:12:38,633
<i>when a friend</i>
<i>showed him around the</i> azucarera.

206
00:12:40,427 --> 00:12:43,263
Oh, okay. Okay. Thank you.

207
00:12:54,107 --> 00:12:57,777
Your guy got the phone already?

208
00:12:58,487 --> 00:12:59,738
<i>Yes.</i>

209
00:12:59,821 --> 00:13:01,615
He told them he's a visitor.

210
00:13:01,698 --> 00:13:04,784
That he had a friend
who worked at the <i>azucarera.</i>

211
00:13:08,330 --> 00:13:10,582
Okay. How's Regina?

212
00:13:13,752 --> 00:13:17,255
She overheard our conversation earlier.

213
00:13:17,964 --> 00:13:19,049
She threw a fit.

214
00:13:19,883 --> 00:13:22,719
<i>We can't make her leave so easily.</i>

215
00:13:25,096 --> 00:13:28,600
Okay, Mara. I'll leave you in charge.
I won't be able to visit for now.

216
00:13:29,267 --> 00:13:30,435
<i>All right, Ben.</i>

217
00:13:31,645 --> 00:13:33,480
Have you talked to your wife?

218
00:13:35,815 --> 00:13:36,983
<i>Not yet.</i>

219
00:13:38,944 --> 00:13:43,615
Just make sure
she doesn't come back here, Ben.

220
00:13:43,698 --> 00:13:45,992
Since Regina and I can't leave for now.

221
00:13:46,826 --> 00:13:47,869
<i>Okay.</i>

222
00:14:01,383 --> 00:14:03,218
Juancho, you made the wrong order.

223
00:14:03,301 --> 00:14:05,220
No, I didn't, Lucy.

224
00:14:05,303 --> 00:14:07,305
That's exactly what you told me.

225
00:14:07,389 --> 00:14:09,349
Why are you arguing with me?

226
00:14:09,432 --> 00:14:11,059
Why are you yelling?

227
00:14:11,142 --> 00:14:13,228
Because you're making it so complicated!

228
00:14:13,311 --> 00:14:14,854
Hey, hey, hey! What's happening here?

229
00:14:14,938 --> 00:14:16,273
What's going on?

230
00:14:16,356 --> 00:14:19,859
Your bartender made the wrong order

231
00:14:19,943 --> 00:14:21,319
and refuses to own up to his mistake.

232
00:14:21,403 --> 00:14:23,446
I just did what she said.

233
00:14:23,530 --> 00:14:24,573
- Excuse me?
- Stop it!

234
00:14:24,656 --> 00:14:26,157
Why did you mess up the order?

235
00:14:26,241 --> 00:14:28,910
Ma'am, have I ever messed up
since I started working here?

236
00:14:28,994 --> 00:14:30,954
- You did just now.
- Ma'am!

237
00:14:31,037 --> 00:14:32,872
Come on, just fix this.

238
00:14:32,956 --> 00:14:34,749
The customer is waiting.

239
00:14:34,833 --> 00:14:37,752
Mind you,
that's coming out of your paycheck.

240
00:14:38,295 --> 00:14:39,462
Ma'am!

241
00:15:27,010 --> 00:15:28,094
Ben.

242
00:15:28,720 --> 00:15:31,139
Ana.

243
00:15:32,349 --> 00:15:33,933
Where have you been?

244
00:15:35,143 --> 00:15:37,646
Uh, after my meeting with the client,

245
00:15:37,729 --> 00:15:40,649
Kat and I went out for wine.

246
00:15:42,025 --> 00:15:43,693
What's happening?
I was worried about you.

247
00:15:43,777 --> 00:15:45,195
You weren't picking up.

248
00:15:45,278 --> 00:15:48,490
Happening to... what, exactly?

249
00:15:48,573 --> 00:15:50,659
Well, I'm just... just worried.

250
00:15:50,742 --> 00:15:51,785
Sorry.

251
00:15:52,577 --> 00:15:54,245
Ana, this has never happened.

252
00:15:54,746 --> 00:15:56,247
Something new, huh?

253
00:15:57,123 --> 00:15:58,958
I can be surprising too.

254
00:16:03,838 --> 00:16:05,757
- Are you okay?
- Yeah.

255
00:16:07,092 --> 00:16:08,426
Are you?

256
00:16:09,886 --> 00:16:11,304
Yeah, I'm okay.

257
00:16:14,683 --> 00:16:17,352
Okay. I'm just happy you're home,
and you're safe.

258
00:16:26,444 --> 00:16:27,529
Oops.

259
00:16:28,113 --> 00:16:30,198
Time to go to work, stranger.

260
00:16:42,585 --> 00:16:44,671
There was no confrontation?

261
00:16:45,755 --> 00:16:47,966
Did you even talk about it?

262
00:16:48,049 --> 00:16:53,555
We talked, but I didn't bring up
the phone or that woman.

263
00:16:54,055 --> 00:16:55,223
But why?

264
00:16:56,349 --> 00:16:59,519
I knew he would make up an excuse.

265
00:16:59,602 --> 00:17:02,522
He would just lie.
So what's the point of bringing it up?

266
00:17:03,064 --> 00:17:04,566
I'm worried for you.

267
00:17:05,608 --> 00:17:09,362
My mother told me
to protect my marriage like my life.

268
00:17:09,446 --> 00:17:10,864
Because it is my life.

269
00:17:11,281 --> 00:17:13,533
- And you are.
- But it's so hard.

270
00:17:13,950 --> 00:17:15,869
I always feel like...

271
00:17:17,245 --> 00:17:20,665
every time I'm close
to finding out the truth,

272
00:17:20,749 --> 00:17:23,835
I end up three steps back.

273
00:17:25,086 --> 00:17:27,338
It's like I'm chasing a ghost.

274
00:17:28,673 --> 00:17:30,842
And that is why I'm worried for you.

275
00:17:31,426 --> 00:17:32,510
Why?

276
00:17:35,847 --> 00:17:36,931
What if...

277
00:17:40,935 --> 00:17:42,020
What if...

278
00:17:42,771 --> 00:17:44,439
this backfires on you?

279
00:17:54,908 --> 00:17:57,368
If you don't want your pay docked,

280
00:17:57,452 --> 00:18:00,038
don't be an idiot like Juancho!

281
00:18:00,121 --> 00:18:02,373
He messed up a simple order!

282
00:18:02,457 --> 00:18:05,084
Boss, I told you, didn't I?

283
00:18:05,168 --> 00:18:06,795
It's not my fault.

284
00:18:06,878 --> 00:18:08,505
How rude of you to talk back to me.

285
00:18:08,588 --> 00:18:10,006
Because you're throwing me under the bus!

286
00:18:10,089 --> 00:18:12,675
And yeah,
because of that, you are fired!

287
00:18:12,759 --> 00:18:14,010
Don't you ever come back here

288
00:18:14,093 --> 00:18:15,261
because that is your final pay!

289
00:18:15,345 --> 00:18:16,930
Boss, please!

290
00:18:17,013 --> 00:18:19,182
- I don't want to hear it.
- Hey, that's not fair!

291
00:18:19,265 --> 00:18:20,725
Juancho did nothing wrong!

292
00:18:20,809 --> 00:18:22,727
- Excuse me?
- You should fire me!

293
00:18:22,811 --> 00:18:24,270
- If you weren't...
- What?

294
00:18:24,354 --> 00:18:27,774
You're so scared to fire me
because I'm a Saguil?

295
00:18:27,857 --> 00:18:29,067
Well then, fine!

296
00:18:29,150 --> 00:18:30,860
I'll resign myself!

297
00:18:30,944 --> 00:18:32,529
I quit!

298
00:18:33,655 --> 00:18:34,739
Lucy!

299
00:18:37,784 --> 00:18:39,786
Hey, Lucy! Wait!

300
00:18:41,663 --> 00:18:43,081
Are you out of your mind?

301
00:18:43,164 --> 00:18:44,874
Why did you quit?
She didn't even fire you!

302
00:18:44,958 --> 00:18:46,209
I don't want to work in a bar anymore!

303
00:18:46,292 --> 00:18:47,502
Go back there!

304
00:18:47,585 --> 00:18:49,963
It's my decision! Leave me alone!

305
00:18:50,046 --> 00:18:54,759
Well, of course you have no idea
how hard it is to find a job because--

306
00:18:54,843 --> 00:18:56,970
Because I'm a Saguil?

307
00:18:57,470 --> 00:19:00,723
Don't you see
that I'm owning up to my actions?

308
00:19:01,307 --> 00:19:06,229
I quit because it's the only way
to make things right!

309
00:19:10,483 --> 00:19:12,819
Bagasse may be our byproduct,

310
00:19:12,902 --> 00:19:16,489
but it can be something
much more useful for us.

311
00:19:17,323 --> 00:19:19,158
What do you think, Attorney?

312
00:19:20,243 --> 00:19:21,661
Very interesting.

313
00:19:23,204 --> 00:19:24,289
I'm very excited.

314
00:19:24,372 --> 00:19:26,958
Even before your presentation...

315
00:19:27,041 --> 00:19:28,877
...I've been on board.

316
00:19:28,960 --> 00:19:33,464
But, um, just give me more time
to think about it.

317
00:19:34,215 --> 00:19:35,633
Then I'll get back to you.

318
00:19:36,217 --> 00:19:37,218
Okay?

319
00:19:37,969 --> 00:19:40,305
Okay?
Anything else for today?

320
00:19:40,388 --> 00:19:42,640
- All right.
- Thank you very much.

321
00:19:42,724 --> 00:19:44,893
Thank you. Have a nice day.
Thank you. Thank you.

322
00:19:44,976 --> 00:19:46,853
I'll get back to you. Yes.

323
00:19:46,936 --> 00:19:48,605
Thank you.

324
00:19:54,569 --> 00:19:55,820
Yes, Attorney.

325
00:19:56,905 --> 00:19:58,907
I hope you have good news for me.

326
00:19:58,990 --> 00:20:00,366
<i>Elizabeth Valdez.</i>

327
00:20:01,951 --> 00:20:04,746
<i>You and your wife</i>
<i>know this woman, don't you?</i>

328
00:20:05,830 --> 00:20:07,749
I saw her at your party.

329
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:10,835
Yeah, she's my PT.

330
00:20:11,419 --> 00:20:13,421
Ana is very fond of her.

331
00:20:14,964 --> 00:20:17,050
Why? What did you find?

332
00:20:20,678 --> 00:20:23,097
She's a loyalty tester.

333
00:20:33,316 --> 00:20:34,484
Understood.

334
00:20:45,662 --> 00:20:46,746
Okay.

335
00:20:48,539 --> 00:20:50,041
Thank you, Attorney.

336
00:21:24,784 --> 00:21:27,370
I've got another one. It's blue!

337
00:21:29,330 --> 00:21:30,999
Say,
"Thank you, Auntie Beth!"

338
00:21:31,082 --> 00:21:32,083
You're welcome!

339
00:21:35,670 --> 00:21:37,422
Thanks for all this.

340
00:21:37,505 --> 00:21:39,465
You're too generous.

341
00:21:39,549 --> 00:21:41,050
Back in Manila,

342
00:21:41,134 --> 00:21:44,470
you'd only buy my son
shirts from roadside shops.

343
00:21:44,554 --> 00:21:45,972
Oh, it's nothing.

344
00:21:47,557 --> 00:21:50,476
I don't always get to buy nice things.

345
00:21:50,810 --> 00:21:54,355
So, I make the most of it
while I still can.

346
00:21:54,981 --> 00:21:56,816
Is that why you don't want to go back?

347
00:21:58,901 --> 00:22:01,654
I found an apartment for you and Caloy.

348
00:22:02,530 --> 00:22:03,865
Do you want to check it out?

349
00:22:03,948 --> 00:22:05,116
An apartment?

350
00:22:06,492 --> 00:22:09,328
Can't we just stay here?

351
00:22:10,163 --> 00:22:11,831
Diane...

352
00:22:12,290 --> 00:22:14,709
We still need to be careful.

353
00:22:14,792 --> 00:22:17,378
Ben comes over here once in a while.

354
00:22:19,338 --> 00:22:21,674
Are we going to talk about this again?

355
00:22:22,467 --> 00:22:26,137
Can't you just tell Ben
that we really are friends?

356
00:22:26,220 --> 00:22:28,556
Just don't mention
the loyalty testing part.

357
00:22:28,639 --> 00:22:30,099
You can't hide it forever.

358
00:22:31,267 --> 00:22:33,686
Diane, everything's going well for me now.

359
00:22:34,270 --> 00:22:37,356
You know, a new place, new acquaintances.

360
00:22:38,816 --> 00:22:41,402
I just don't want to ruin
what I have right now.

361
00:22:42,070 --> 00:22:43,488
You get it, right?

362
00:22:51,120 --> 00:22:53,289
Oh, wait. I have to go.

363
00:22:53,372 --> 00:22:54,582
Where are you going now?

364
00:22:54,665 --> 00:22:56,876
I just need to be somewhere.
I'll be back in a bit.

365
00:22:56,959 --> 00:22:58,711
Caloy, see you later!

366
00:22:59,796 --> 00:23:00,797
Bye.

367
00:23:13,267 --> 00:23:14,685
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

368
00:23:25,863 --> 00:23:26,697
Beth!

369
00:23:29,242 --> 00:23:30,243
Attorney!

370
00:23:38,584 --> 00:23:40,336
What are you doing here?

371
00:23:43,381 --> 00:23:46,217
Attorney... coffee beans.

372
00:23:46,300 --> 00:23:47,218
For you.

373
00:23:47,301 --> 00:23:49,220
Coffee beans?
What's-- What for?

374
00:23:50,138 --> 00:23:52,890
Just to thank you for everything.

375
00:23:53,683 --> 00:23:54,934
Thank you?

376
00:23:58,229 --> 00:24:01,232
Didn't you just treat me and Ana?

377
00:24:02,066 --> 00:24:04,318
But I don't think it was enough.

378
00:24:04,402 --> 00:24:05,695
So, yeah.

379
00:24:06,028 --> 00:24:08,865
Okay. Wow. Thank you.

380
00:24:10,032 --> 00:24:11,367
Thank you very much.

381
00:24:13,744 --> 00:24:14,829
This is nice.

382
00:24:14,912 --> 00:24:17,623
Attorney,
I just wanted to ask you something.

383
00:24:17,707 --> 00:24:18,791
Sure.

384
00:24:20,084 --> 00:24:22,253
I think I saw you yesterday.

385
00:24:23,504 --> 00:24:24,505
Me?

386
00:24:25,423 --> 00:24:26,507
Yeah.

387
00:24:26,966 --> 00:24:28,885
Around our area.

388
00:24:28,968 --> 00:24:31,637
I think I saw your car.

389
00:24:32,346 --> 00:24:33,347
This car?

390
00:24:35,308 --> 00:24:36,142
Yes, this car.

391
00:24:38,519 --> 00:24:39,937
Where was I yesterday?

392
00:24:40,354 --> 00:24:42,773
I did some personal errands in town.

393
00:24:43,733 --> 00:24:46,986
And then, I went to the <i>azucarera.</i>

394
00:24:50,489 --> 00:24:51,407
That's all.

395
00:24:53,326 --> 00:24:54,368
Ah...

396
00:24:55,953 --> 00:24:58,039
I'm probably just mistaken.

397
00:24:59,957 --> 00:25:01,125
That's okay.

398
00:25:01,209 --> 00:25:02,460
You know what they say.

399
00:25:04,545 --> 00:25:07,882
When you think
you saw someone who wasn't there,

400
00:25:09,342 --> 00:25:11,010
it means you've been thinking of them.

401
00:25:14,639 --> 00:25:15,640
Or...

402
00:25:16,224 --> 00:25:17,725
they've been thinking of you.

403
00:25:20,186 --> 00:25:23,022
So, which is which?

404
00:25:25,441 --> 00:25:27,944
Maybe I was just
thinking of you, Attorney.

405
00:25:29,612 --> 00:25:31,614
- All right, I'll be on my way.
- Beth.

406
00:25:35,076 --> 00:25:36,827
Why don't I give you a ride?

407
00:25:40,373 --> 00:25:41,791
- But...
- Come on!

408
00:25:58,474 --> 00:26:00,851
You and your son are stupid!

409
00:26:00,935 --> 00:26:02,770
So, Juancho and Lucy are working together?

410
00:26:02,853 --> 00:26:04,397
They're still connected!

411
00:26:04,480 --> 00:26:06,065
My son just works there.

412
00:26:06,148 --> 00:26:07,316
That's another thing!

413
00:26:07,692 --> 00:26:09,694
Why is he working outside?

414
00:26:09,777 --> 00:26:13,030
Is he trying to avoid
his responsibilities here?

415
00:26:13,364 --> 00:26:14,782
He's not avoiding anything.

416
00:26:15,366 --> 00:26:17,451
Just turn me into your slave
instead of him.

417
00:26:17,535 --> 00:26:20,955
Wow, Reynaldo!

418
00:26:21,414 --> 00:26:24,834
You're the most fit person
to do things in this house!

419
00:26:24,917 --> 00:26:27,670
Your son is in perfect condition to--

420
00:26:27,753 --> 00:26:30,214
To what? To be your slave?

421
00:26:30,798 --> 00:26:33,968
Imelda, you don't have the right
to punish my son.

422
00:26:34,385 --> 00:26:35,970
He's innocent.

423
00:26:36,387 --> 00:26:37,805
Just punish me instead.

424
00:26:37,888 --> 00:26:40,391
I'd rather punish your son.

425
00:26:41,142 --> 00:26:42,518
I want him to experience

426
00:26:42,601 --> 00:26:44,687
the hardships
that my children had to go through.

427
00:26:44,770 --> 00:26:47,440
Your Juancho had you at your best

428
00:26:47,523 --> 00:26:50,609
while my Ana and Sam were miserable
without a father.

429
00:26:50,693 --> 00:26:51,944
That's not fair.

430
00:26:52,028 --> 00:26:53,279
Fair?

431
00:26:53,362 --> 00:26:55,239
Now you want to talk fairness? Fine!

432
00:26:55,323 --> 00:26:58,993
Then,
I'll punish both you and your son.

433
00:26:59,076 --> 00:27:00,494
Just wait and see.

434
00:27:00,578 --> 00:27:02,747
<i>Don't leave the house yet.</i>

435
00:27:02,830 --> 00:27:04,332
<i>- I'm on my way home.</i>

436
00:27:21,223 --> 00:27:22,224
Beth?

437
00:27:24,769 --> 00:27:25,770
Attorney?

438
00:27:39,575 --> 00:27:40,826
Seat belt.

439
00:27:45,331 --> 00:27:47,249
T-Thank you.

440
00:27:49,627 --> 00:27:50,961
So, where should we go?

441
00:27:51,796 --> 00:27:52,797
What?

442
00:27:53,964 --> 00:27:56,133
Where should we go?

443
00:27:56,217 --> 00:27:58,886
You said you're going back
to the apartment.

444
00:27:59,929 --> 00:28:01,055
Is that right?

445
00:28:02,014 --> 00:28:03,182
I...

446
00:28:03,766 --> 00:28:06,102
There's somewhere I need to go to first.

447
00:28:07,895 --> 00:28:08,979
Okay.

448
00:28:09,980 --> 00:28:12,691
I'll drive you there, then...

449
00:28:13,192 --> 00:28:14,944
- I'll take you home.
- No.

450
00:28:18,989 --> 00:28:20,658
Hey, Beth.
What's wrong?

451
00:28:20,741 --> 00:28:22,660
No, Attorney, it's just...

452
00:28:22,743 --> 00:28:24,453
You don't have to.

453
00:28:24,537 --> 00:28:25,871
I'll be fine.

454
00:28:29,208 --> 00:28:31,210
No, it's okay.

455
00:28:31,585 --> 00:28:33,003
You're so funny.

456
00:28:33,421 --> 00:28:34,672
Why are you so nervous?

457
00:28:37,591 --> 00:28:38,843
Just relax.

458
00:28:40,970 --> 00:28:42,221
I got you.

459
00:28:42,304 --> 00:28:44,056
I've got some spare time.

460
00:28:44,140 --> 00:28:46,058
Ana isn't home yet.

461
00:28:53,107 --> 00:28:54,191
Ready?

462
00:28:54,859 --> 00:28:55,943
Yeah.

463
00:28:59,864 --> 00:29:02,116
- Juancho.
- Pa.

464
00:29:03,492 --> 00:29:04,827
Why are you home so soon?

465
00:29:05,870 --> 00:29:07,621
Aren't you in the opening shift?

466
00:29:10,416 --> 00:29:12,334
I just got fired, Pa.

467
00:29:13,627 --> 00:29:16,714
Huh? Why? What happened?

468
00:29:17,423 --> 00:29:19,091
Finally!

469
00:29:19,425 --> 00:29:21,260
Good news for today.

470
00:29:21,802 --> 00:29:24,805
You can't spend time
with Mariano's granddaughter anymore.

471
00:29:27,933 --> 00:29:29,768
I'll be in my room.

472
00:29:30,728 --> 00:29:31,979
Excuse me.

473
00:29:38,611 --> 00:29:40,946
Did you have anything to do with this?

474
00:29:43,032 --> 00:29:47,036
Reynaldo,
I can do much worse than that.

475
00:29:47,119 --> 00:29:49,538
But I don't.

476
00:29:49,830 --> 00:29:52,416
Because I don't want
people talking about me

477
00:29:52,500 --> 00:29:54,752
being that evil stepmother.

478
00:29:56,462 --> 00:29:58,130
I hope you're happy now.

479
00:30:03,135 --> 00:30:06,138
No. That's not enough.

480
00:30:10,017 --> 00:30:12,770
Ah, Attorney, thanks for driving me here.

481
00:30:13,187 --> 00:30:14,855
You're most welcome.

482
00:30:15,648 --> 00:30:17,816
I'll wait for you to leave.

483
00:30:17,900 --> 00:30:20,069
No, I'll wait for you to get inside.

484
00:30:21,153 --> 00:30:23,405
Attorney, you don't have to.

485
00:30:23,489 --> 00:30:25,491
My apartment is just a few steps away.

486
00:30:25,574 --> 00:30:26,784
That's the thing, Beth.

487
00:30:26,867 --> 00:30:28,285
You'll never know.

488
00:30:28,369 --> 00:30:29,954
Sometimes,
you think you're already safe,

489
00:30:30,037 --> 00:30:31,664
but suddenly, something bad happens.

490
00:30:34,250 --> 00:30:35,834
You don't have to scare me like that.

491
00:30:35,918 --> 00:30:38,337
No, no. I'm just saying...

492
00:30:38,420 --> 00:30:40,339
always be careful, Beth.

493
00:30:46,262 --> 00:30:49,765
<i>I have a right to my son,</i>
<i>so this isn't kidnapping.</i>

494
00:30:58,899 --> 00:31:00,317
- Thank you.
- Okay.

495
00:31:18,586 --> 00:31:23,090
I think that apartment's better
than the one you showed me before.

496
00:31:24,049 --> 00:31:26,135
But it's still so close to me.

497
00:31:30,931 --> 00:31:34,184
Be honest. You just want me and Caloy
out of here, right?

498
00:31:35,686 --> 00:31:39,440
It's not that. I just thought
if you and Caloy move to Vallente,

499
00:31:39,523 --> 00:31:42,276
Mike might become a bigger problem to you.

500
00:31:42,693 --> 00:31:45,195
Beth, he's trying
to take my son away from me.

501
00:31:45,279 --> 00:31:48,699
If we go back to Manila,
I might never see this kid again.

502
00:31:49,116 --> 00:31:52,703
You're overreacting.
I'm just trying to be nice.

503
00:31:54,288 --> 00:31:55,456
Just admit it.

504
00:31:55,539 --> 00:31:57,708
You want to continue flirting
with that attorney.

505
00:31:58,417 --> 00:32:00,002
And you can't do that with us here.

506
00:32:01,879 --> 00:32:03,964
What are you talking about?

507
00:32:04,048 --> 00:32:05,466
My God.

508
00:32:06,383 --> 00:32:08,385
I saw you smiling outside.

509
00:32:08,469 --> 00:32:10,638
I know what that smile means.

510
00:32:11,096 --> 00:32:12,348
Goodness, Beth.

511
00:32:12,431 --> 00:32:14,266
You know he's married.

512
00:32:14,350 --> 00:32:16,810
That smile meant nothing.

513
00:32:18,604 --> 00:32:20,606
It's not just a smile.

514
00:32:20,689 --> 00:32:22,524
We both know how you are.

515
00:32:22,608 --> 00:32:26,111
The last time you smiled that way,
you were head over heels for a guy.

516
00:32:31,075 --> 00:32:32,826
All right. We'll just leave then.

517
00:32:32,910 --> 00:32:34,495
I'll take that apartment
you were talking about,

518
00:32:34,578 --> 00:32:36,580
so we won't be a nuisance to you.

519
00:32:37,623 --> 00:32:39,458
- Son...
- Diane, wait.

520
00:32:39,541 --> 00:32:40,959
No, it's okay. I get it.

521
00:32:44,046 --> 00:32:45,047
Diane...

522
00:32:57,476 --> 00:33:00,396
There's a newly opened restaurant

523
00:33:00,479 --> 00:33:01,814
on Esplanade Street.

524
00:33:02,648 --> 00:33:04,566
It's my friend Patty's.

525
00:33:05,109 --> 00:33:06,110
Okay.

526
00:33:07,236 --> 00:33:09,238
- Patty?
- Mm-hmm.

527
00:33:11,073 --> 00:33:12,074
Patty...

528
00:33:12,783 --> 00:33:14,118
Who's Patty?

529
00:33:14,660 --> 00:33:18,330
Oh, you haven't met her
because she just got back from the UK.

530
00:33:19,039 --> 00:33:20,374
Let's have dinner there.

531
00:33:21,291 --> 00:33:22,459
Sure.

532
00:33:22,543 --> 00:33:24,211
Of course. Let's go.

533
00:33:25,337 --> 00:33:27,840
Um... are you sure?

534
00:33:27,923 --> 00:33:31,093
If you're busy,
I can just go with Katrina instead.

535
00:33:31,176 --> 00:33:33,762
It's okay.

536
00:33:40,185 --> 00:33:42,271
I always have time for you.

537
00:33:43,981 --> 00:33:45,733
Should I pick you up from the atelier?

538
00:33:46,525 --> 00:33:47,943
No, it's okay.

539
00:33:48,026 --> 00:33:51,029
I have a meeting
with a client in Capistrano,

540
00:33:51,113 --> 00:33:53,115
so I'll just see you there.

541
00:33:53,532 --> 00:33:55,367
It's more efficient.

542
00:33:55,701 --> 00:33:57,369
- Okay.
- I'll get ready for bed.

543
00:33:57,453 --> 00:33:58,454
Okay.

544
00:34:38,243 --> 00:34:40,412
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

545
00:34:40,954 --> 00:34:44,082
- Ma'am, Attorney, good morning.
- Morning, Beth.

546
00:34:45,959 --> 00:34:48,545
It's your last PT session today, right?

547
00:34:49,087 --> 00:34:50,339
Yes, ma'am.

548
00:34:50,839 --> 00:34:53,008
Okay. I'll go ahead.

549
00:34:53,467 --> 00:34:55,219
Don't forget dinner later.

550
00:34:55,302 --> 00:34:56,553
No, I won't.

551
00:34:58,597 --> 00:34:59,681
Ana?

552
00:35:02,309 --> 00:35:03,477
Have a nice day.

553
00:35:14,279 --> 00:35:16,031
- Nanny.
- Ready, Beth?

554
00:35:21,703 --> 00:35:22,704
Yeah.

555
00:35:22,788 --> 00:35:24,456
It's good, but I think there's...

556
00:35:25,791 --> 00:35:26,875
- a bit--
- You feel any pain?

557
00:35:26,959 --> 00:35:29,044
No. A little pinch.

558
00:35:29,127 --> 00:35:30,629
Like, here.

559
00:35:30,712 --> 00:35:31,839
- Here?
- Yeah.

560
00:35:31,922 --> 00:35:33,257
What's the pain level, Attorney?

561
00:35:33,340 --> 00:35:35,509
Uh... it's not too bad.

562
00:35:35,592 --> 00:35:36,677
It's just a bit...

563
00:35:37,219 --> 00:35:38,887
uncomfortable.

564
00:35:40,180 --> 00:35:42,349
- There.
- Here?

565
00:35:42,432 --> 00:35:44,017
Uh, lower.

566
00:35:44,726 --> 00:35:45,811
Here?

567
00:35:46,478 --> 00:35:47,563
Lower.

568
00:35:48,397 --> 00:35:50,315
A little bit to the side.

569
00:35:50,399 --> 00:35:52,067
- Here?
- Can I help you?

570
00:35:53,026 --> 00:35:54,236
Sure.

571
00:35:54,319 --> 00:35:55,487
Here.

572
00:35:56,405 --> 00:35:58,073
It starts here.

573
00:35:59,074 --> 00:36:01,577
Actually, this is affected.

574
00:36:02,828 --> 00:36:03,912
Right here.

575
00:36:04,705 --> 00:36:06,039
There.

576
00:36:06,123 --> 00:36:08,292
This whole muscle.

577
00:36:08,375 --> 00:36:10,043
This whole muscle here, Beth.

578
00:36:10,878 --> 00:36:12,629
Yeah. Because I think...

579
00:36:15,591 --> 00:36:17,342
the pain crawls up here.

580
00:36:24,099 --> 00:36:25,434
From here...

581
00:36:26,602 --> 00:36:27,686
to there.

582
00:36:28,478 --> 00:36:29,897
From here...

583
00:36:29,980 --> 00:36:31,315
to here.

584
00:36:34,109 --> 00:36:35,110
Does it hurt?

585
00:36:36,320 --> 00:36:37,738
You're a big help.

586
00:36:45,370 --> 00:36:47,372
I'm going to miss you, Attorney.

587
00:36:52,336 --> 00:36:53,921
I'm going to miss you too.

588
00:36:58,800 --> 00:37:01,470
I'll miss how you help me
heal my shoulders.

589
00:37:07,225 --> 00:37:08,644
I'm going to miss this.

590
00:37:15,400 --> 00:37:16,818
I feel better.

591
00:37:22,032 --> 00:37:24,368
- Y-You feel okay now?
- Yeah.

592
00:37:28,455 --> 00:37:29,498
Yeah.

593
00:37:35,921 --> 00:37:37,089
Okay, Beth.

594
00:37:39,007 --> 00:37:41,009
I have to get ready for work.

595
00:37:41,093 --> 00:37:43,679
Hey, thanks again. Okay?

596
00:37:46,264 --> 00:37:48,016
I'll ask the driver to drive you home.

597
00:37:48,850 --> 00:37:50,268
There's no need. I'll be fine.

598
00:37:50,352 --> 00:37:52,688
No, I insist. Okay?

599
00:37:55,816 --> 00:37:57,401
All right. Thank you.

600
00:37:58,610 --> 00:38:01,196
Okay. Thanks again.

601
00:38:04,199 --> 00:38:05,534
Thank you so much, Beth.

602
00:38:06,994 --> 00:38:08,078
Okay.

603
00:38:11,665 --> 00:38:13,750
It'll really catch your attention.

604
00:38:19,881 --> 00:38:22,884
It's a beautiful picture
of Attorney and Ana.

605
00:38:25,262 --> 00:38:26,930
It's really beautiful.

606
00:38:36,314 --> 00:38:39,151
The driver is outside.
He's waiting for you.

607
00:38:39,693 --> 00:38:41,778
Okay, Nanny Cedes, thank you.

608
00:38:42,320 --> 00:38:43,447
I'm going to miss you.

609
00:38:43,530 --> 00:38:44,698
Mm-hmm.

610
00:38:46,199 --> 00:38:48,952
I wish I lived here.

611
00:38:49,411 --> 00:38:52,164
Come on.

612
00:39:16,897 --> 00:39:18,648
Hello, Mara.

613
00:39:19,983 --> 00:39:21,902
Have you talked to your wife?

614
00:39:23,528 --> 00:39:25,197
She's a smart woman, Ben.

615
00:39:26,073 --> 00:39:27,657
<i>Don't worry about it.</i>

616
00:39:28,992 --> 00:39:30,494
I came up with a plan.

617
00:39:31,328 --> 00:39:32,412
<i>Tell me.</i>

618
00:39:40,545 --> 00:39:42,130
I know a way...

619
00:39:43,423 --> 00:39:45,008
to make her stop.

620
00:39:47,552 --> 00:39:50,180
Ben, it's normal for a woman
to have suspicions.

621
00:39:51,264 --> 00:39:52,432
I know.

622
00:39:55,143 --> 00:39:56,645
I'll take care of it.

623
00:39:57,020 --> 00:39:59,022
Just look after my sister, will you?

624
00:39:59,106 --> 00:40:00,857
<i>Don't worry.</i>

625
00:40:03,110 --> 00:40:05,862
Your sister didn't see Ana.

626
00:41:01,209 --> 00:41:03,461
- Hello?
- <i>Hi.</i>

627
00:41:04,087 --> 00:41:05,255
I'm here.

628
00:41:05,338 --> 00:41:06,756
<i>Hi. Oh, no.</i>

629
00:41:07,465 --> 00:41:09,551
<i>My meeting is running late.</i>

630
00:41:10,093 --> 00:41:11,261
Oh, that's okay.

631
00:41:11,803 --> 00:41:12,888
I'll wait for you.

632
00:41:14,097 --> 00:41:16,766
No, I think this will take a while.

633
00:41:17,058 --> 00:41:19,728
I'm so sorry, love.
I think I have to rain check.

634
00:41:20,896 --> 00:41:22,898
Oh, I see. Okay, so...

635
00:41:24,107 --> 00:41:25,525
I'll just see you at home?

636
00:41:27,235 --> 00:41:30,739
Yeah, okay. All right.
I'll see you later, okay? Sorry.

637
00:41:32,324 --> 00:41:33,408
Okay.

638
00:41:34,743 --> 00:41:36,578
Okay, no problem. Bye, I love you.

639
00:42:56,491 --> 00:42:58,326
<i>Are you out of your mind?</i>

640
00:42:58,410 --> 00:42:59,703
Don't you get it?

641
00:42:59,786 --> 00:43:01,454
Now that I canceled our dinner plans,

642
00:43:01,538 --> 00:43:03,665
he'll meet with his mistress.

643
00:43:03,748 --> 00:43:07,669
See? He said he's going home,
but this isn't the way home.

644
00:43:07,752 --> 00:43:09,421
I know what that means.

645
00:43:09,504 --> 00:43:12,340
My question is,
why are you doing that to yourself?

646
00:43:12,424 --> 00:43:15,135
I need to catch them in the act

647
00:43:15,218 --> 00:43:18,138
because that will be my proof
that he's cheating on me!

648
00:43:18,221 --> 00:43:19,723
<i>But you're alone.</i>

649
00:43:20,348 --> 00:43:21,516
Fine, Ana, tell me.

650
00:43:21,599 --> 00:43:25,145
If you see them like how you want,
will you be able to handle it?

651
00:43:25,228 --> 00:43:26,855
I don't know, okay?
I don't know.

652
00:43:26,938 --> 00:43:29,274
I need to catch them in the act.

653
00:43:29,357 --> 00:43:30,275
<i>Please.</i>

654
00:43:30,734 --> 00:43:33,403
Do not do anything that will ruin you.

655
00:43:33,486 --> 00:43:35,113
You shouldn't be doing this to yourself.

656
00:43:35,196 --> 00:43:36,948
You are Ana Madrigal,
for goodness' sake!

657
00:43:37,032 --> 00:43:39,784
Exactly! I am Ana Madrigal!

658
00:43:39,868 --> 00:43:42,454
They can't just make a fool out of me!

659
00:44:04,851 --> 00:44:06,269
Attorney!

660
00:44:18,740 --> 00:44:20,075
Beth.

661
00:44:20,158 --> 00:44:21,534
You're here too?

662
00:44:21,618 --> 00:44:22,786
Yeah.

663
00:44:22,869 --> 00:44:24,162
Oh, Attorney.

664
00:44:24,245 --> 00:44:25,914
You asked me to come here.

665
00:44:26,456 --> 00:44:27,707
What?

666
00:44:27,791 --> 00:44:29,626
Yeah. Yeah, here.

667
00:44:31,544 --> 00:44:32,712
That's you.

668
00:44:34,672 --> 00:44:35,882
Oh, my God.

669
00:44:37,509 --> 00:44:40,095
Oh, I'm... I'm sorry.

670
00:44:40,178 --> 00:44:42,263
So this is why Ana isn't replying.

671
00:44:44,808 --> 00:44:46,309
Oh, I sent it to you.

672
00:44:46,393 --> 00:44:47,227
I'm so sorry.

673
00:44:47,310 --> 00:44:48,728
I wish you had texted me back,

674
00:44:48,812 --> 00:44:50,438
so you wouldn't have bothered to come.

675
00:44:50,855 --> 00:44:53,858
You're silly, Attorney.

676
00:44:54,401 --> 00:44:58,571
I thought you wouldn't have texted me
if you didn't want to hang out.

677
00:44:59,364 --> 00:45:00,448
Right?

678
00:45:04,077 --> 00:45:05,161
Um...

679
00:45:06,162 --> 00:45:07,997
Well, I don't mind fishing with you.

680
00:45:10,333 --> 00:45:11,584
What's that for?

681
00:45:12,961 --> 00:45:15,463
I'll store my catch in here.

682
00:45:16,047 --> 00:45:19,050
I didn't know you could do that.
That thing on top.

683
00:45:22,679 --> 00:45:24,347
To keep the fish from escaping.

684
00:45:26,558 --> 00:45:27,809
That's awesome.

685
00:45:28,309 --> 00:45:29,477
DIY. Cool.

686
00:45:30,687 --> 00:45:33,273
It just needs a rope.

687
00:45:38,653 --> 00:45:39,821
Okay.

688
00:45:40,655 --> 00:45:41,656
Ready.

689
00:45:49,581 --> 00:45:51,082
You're funny, Attorney.

690
00:46:02,218 --> 00:46:05,054
That wasn't mine. I just read it online.

691
00:46:08,725 --> 00:46:11,978
You know what, if Harry, my brother,
hears your joke,

692
00:46:12,479 --> 00:46:14,147
you'll get along well.

693
00:46:14,856 --> 00:46:16,357
You guys have the same humor.

694
00:46:16,441 --> 00:46:18,193
Are you saying I'm corny?

695
00:46:19,068 --> 00:46:20,403
It's okay, you can say it.

696
00:46:20,487 --> 00:46:24,240
No, Attorney. I wish
you could hang out with my siblings.

697
00:46:25,492 --> 00:46:26,993
Because I'm sure

698
00:46:27,076 --> 00:46:29,412
you'd be a good older brother to them.

699
00:46:29,913 --> 00:46:31,915
- Oh, yeah?
- Mm.

700
00:46:32,874 --> 00:46:34,459
Yeah, I'd love to meet them.

701
00:46:35,502 --> 00:46:38,254
Fine by me.
I can be there for them.

702
00:46:39,255 --> 00:46:40,256
Really?

703
00:46:40,632 --> 00:46:41,883
Yeah, Beth.

704
00:46:42,675 --> 00:46:44,177
We've grown close.

705
00:46:44,677 --> 00:46:48,097
So your loved ones,
the important people in your life,

706
00:46:48,181 --> 00:46:49,682
are important to me too.

707
00:46:56,856 --> 00:46:57,941
You need these?

708
00:47:00,276 --> 00:47:02,529
Oh, I'm good. Don't worry.

709
00:47:02,862 --> 00:47:04,948
Tch. Okay.

710
00:47:22,382 --> 00:47:24,384
Beth, will you look at me?

711
00:47:26,302 --> 00:47:27,387
Huh?

712
00:47:30,265 --> 00:47:32,517
May I? Just look here.

713
00:47:33,601 --> 00:47:35,728
What's that?
Is that from charcoal?

714
00:47:36,729 --> 00:47:38,940
- Charcoal, Attorney?
- How did that get there?

715
00:47:39,023 --> 00:47:41,818
Were you grilling?

716
00:47:41,901 --> 00:47:43,152
Thank you, Attorney.

717
00:47:50,868 --> 00:47:52,287
Oops. Did you see that?

718
00:47:52,370 --> 00:47:54,831
- Oh! Attorney, come on!
- Did you see that? Go!

719
00:47:54,914 --> 00:47:56,416
Go, go.

720
00:47:56,749 --> 00:47:57,917
I think we got a big one.

721
00:47:58,001 --> 00:47:59,335
Go, go, go, go, go!

722
00:47:59,419 --> 00:48:01,045
Yeah, release it a little.

723
00:48:07,260 --> 00:48:09,470
There.
Just be patient. Just be patient.

724
00:48:09,554 --> 00:48:11,389
It already took your bait.

725
00:48:11,973 --> 00:48:13,891
You got this. You can do it, Beth.

726
00:48:14,225 --> 00:48:15,893
Always remember, Beth,

727
00:48:16,394 --> 00:48:19,981
there are three reasons
why a fish grabs your bait.

728
00:48:21,899 --> 00:48:23,735
Just hold it. Keep it steady.

729
00:48:24,527 --> 00:48:27,280
Number one,
hunger, obviously.

730
00:48:27,989 --> 00:48:29,991
Go. Don't let go. Don't let go.

731
00:48:30,450 --> 00:48:33,202
Two, curiosity. Okay?

732
00:48:41,377 --> 00:48:43,880
Something unfamiliar draws it closer.

733
00:48:50,970 --> 00:48:52,221
Three.

734
00:48:53,473 --> 00:48:54,724
Territory.

735
00:49:00,021 --> 00:49:01,856
Remember that, Beth.

736
00:49:38,643 --> 00:49:39,977
Beth...

737
00:49:43,606 --> 00:49:46,025
Sorry, Attorney. I thought...

738
00:49:47,235 --> 00:49:50,488
Sorry, Attorney. I didn't really mean to.

739
00:49:51,447 --> 00:49:52,615
I'm really sorry.

740
00:49:52,699 --> 00:49:54,117
I'm married, Beth.

741
00:49:56,202 --> 00:49:57,537
I know that.

742
00:49:59,580 --> 00:50:01,582
I'm really sorry, Attorney.

743
00:50:21,060 --> 00:50:23,312
Actually,
I think I'd better go.

744
00:51:11,736 --> 00:51:14,864
No, no, no!

745
00:51:14,947 --> 00:51:16,115
No!

746
00:51:16,199 --> 00:51:18,075
No, no, no!

747
00:51:18,159 --> 00:51:19,410
Liar!

748
00:51:19,494 --> 00:51:20,953
Liar!

749
00:51:24,415 --> 00:51:25,666
He's a liar!

750
00:51:26,459 --> 00:51:27,877
Liar!

751
00:51:39,972 --> 00:51:41,057
Hey.

752
00:51:42,934 --> 00:51:44,268
Long day?

753
00:51:46,687 --> 00:51:49,690
Yes.

754
00:51:55,321 --> 00:51:56,823
Not too close, Ben.

755
00:51:58,324 --> 00:51:59,325
Okay.

756
00:52:01,285 --> 00:52:02,286
Okay.

757
00:52:02,620 --> 00:52:04,038
Okay, good night.

758
00:52:40,825 --> 00:52:42,660
<i>That's quite bold of you.</i>

759
00:52:46,038 --> 00:52:48,207
Flirting with a married man.

760
00:52:51,836 --> 00:52:54,505
I didn't mean to fall for your husband.

761
00:52:55,923 --> 00:52:57,091
It just happened.

762
00:52:57,174 --> 00:52:58,593
"Just happened"?

763
00:52:59,218 --> 00:53:00,636
Or did you plan it?

764
00:53:01,178 --> 00:53:02,430
It wasn't planned.

765
00:53:03,264 --> 00:53:04,599
I didn't mean to.

766
00:53:05,683 --> 00:53:07,101
Oh, come on, Beth.

767
00:53:07,894 --> 00:53:08,936
For all I know,

768
00:53:09,020 --> 00:53:12,189
you make moves on clients
you want for yourself.

769
00:53:13,482 --> 00:53:14,984
Didn't you push me to do this?

770
00:53:16,193 --> 00:53:18,613
I've stopped doing
loyalty testing, remember?

771
00:53:19,363 --> 00:53:20,865
Cut to the chase.

772
00:53:20,948 --> 00:53:22,825
You're the one
who put me in this situation.

773
00:53:23,242 --> 00:53:25,244
So it's my fault now?

774
00:53:25,661 --> 00:53:28,080
- Yes.
- You're shameless.

775
00:53:28,164 --> 00:53:29,540
I know.

776
00:53:29,624 --> 00:53:32,001
But you can't hide the fact

777
00:53:32,084 --> 00:53:34,921
that you're the one
who pushed us together.

778
00:53:35,713 --> 00:53:37,381
So if there's anyone to blame,

779
00:53:37,798 --> 00:53:40,384
it's no one but you.

780
00:53:40,801 --> 00:53:41,802
Go on!

781
00:53:42,386 --> 00:53:43,220
Go on.

782
00:53:43,596 --> 00:53:44,597
Do it.

783
00:53:46,182 --> 00:53:49,185
And I'll tell Ben everything you did.

784
00:53:51,228 --> 00:53:54,649
Because between us two, you, Ana...

785
00:53:56,525 --> 00:53:58,527
are the loser.

786
00:54:34,730 --> 00:54:36,732
<i>She's a loyalty tester.</i>

787
00:54:37,108 --> 00:54:38,526
Loyalty tester?

788
00:54:39,318 --> 00:54:42,071
<i>These people are hired to check</i>

789
00:54:42,571 --> 00:54:45,574
<i>if their partners are loyal to them.</i>

790
00:54:46,993 --> 00:54:48,327
That's a job?

791
00:54:49,370 --> 00:54:50,329
<i>Yes.</i>

792
00:54:51,747 --> 00:54:53,666
It's an online thing.

793
00:54:53,749 --> 00:54:57,962
I'm having people trace
Elizabeth and Diane's online accounts.

794
00:54:58,713 --> 00:55:02,383
<i>And a viral video of a man popped up.</i>

795
00:55:03,050 --> 00:55:05,386
"She's a loyalty tester
my girlfriend hired to flirt with me..."

796
00:55:05,469 --> 00:55:06,470
<i>His name is Ryan.</i>

797
00:55:06,554 --> 00:55:10,599
<i>He was furious</i>
<i>because of Diane's loyalty check.</i>

798
00:55:10,683 --> 00:55:13,019
<i>Damn you! You slut!</i>

799
00:55:13,519 --> 00:55:14,854
<i>You're the criminal!</i>

800
00:55:16,105 --> 00:55:18,858
Wait. So they deceive people?

801
00:55:19,942 --> 00:55:21,360
<i>You could say that.</i>

802
00:55:21,444 --> 00:55:26,532
I spoke to Ryan,
and he wanted to sue Diane for fraud.

803
00:55:26,615 --> 00:55:31,912
However, due to the assault that happened,
I told him that he could also be charged.

804
00:55:33,080 --> 00:55:34,665
So-- Okay.

805
00:55:35,332 --> 00:55:37,001
So, how does the whole thing go?

806
00:55:37,543 --> 00:55:39,712
They will send you an online message.

807
00:55:41,172 --> 00:55:42,339
And then,

808
00:55:42,423 --> 00:55:44,425
they will try to connect.

809
00:55:45,217 --> 00:55:48,512
<i>Hi! I knew you were</i>
<i>the one I saw in suggested friends.</i>

810
00:55:48,596 --> 00:55:50,347
<i>Attorney, hello!</i>

811
00:55:50,431 --> 00:55:51,682
<i>Thank you for accepting.</i>

812
00:55:53,184 --> 00:55:55,269
<i>And they will flirt with you.</i>

813
00:55:56,562 --> 00:55:58,189
Can you give me a ride?

814
00:55:58,272 --> 00:55:59,565
<i>Until you end up saying...</i>

815
00:56:00,775 --> 00:56:02,359
- Attorney!
<i>- ...you are not single.</i>

816
00:56:02,443 --> 00:56:04,361
- Yes?
- Let's get coffee.

817
00:56:04,445 --> 00:56:06,655
<i>If the guy turned them down,</i>

818
00:56:07,239 --> 00:56:08,991
<i>then they passed the test.</i>

819
00:56:09,075 --> 00:56:10,367
<i>They're loyal.</i>

820
00:56:10,451 --> 00:56:11,619
<i>But if they gave in,</i>

821
00:56:11,702 --> 00:56:13,079
<i>then they failed.</i>

822
00:56:13,162 --> 00:56:14,705
Oh, my God!

823
00:56:14,789 --> 00:56:16,040
- Sir!
- I'm so sorry.

824
00:56:16,123 --> 00:56:18,501
- I thought you were my wife. I'm sorry.
- I'm really sorry.

825
00:56:18,584 --> 00:56:20,669
- No. What are you doing here?
- I'm sorry.

826
00:56:20,753 --> 00:56:22,588
Ma'am, I'm sorry.

827
00:56:28,177 --> 00:56:30,763
Ana put me on a loyalty test.

828
00:56:32,598 --> 00:56:34,517
Are you cheating on her?

829
00:56:35,309 --> 00:56:36,477
No.

830
00:56:37,186 --> 00:56:39,188
<i>Then she's starting to become suspicious.</i>

831
00:56:39,980 --> 00:56:42,399
Right now, she thinks
there's a woman involved.

832
00:56:42,983 --> 00:56:45,820
But once she realizes that's not the case,

833
00:56:46,487 --> 00:56:49,156
she'll become suspicious of other things.

834
00:56:50,533 --> 00:56:52,785
<i>You need to fix this, Ben.</i>

835
00:56:53,744 --> 00:56:57,331
<i>The skeletons from your past</i>
<i>can be dug up.</i>

836
00:56:58,249 --> 00:57:00,334
And I don't want to be involved, Ben.

837
00:57:06,966 --> 00:57:08,217
Understood.

838
00:57:19,311 --> 00:57:20,312
Okay.

839
00:57:22,189 --> 00:57:23,691
Thank you, Attorney.

840
00:57:30,739 --> 00:57:34,160
Uh, sir.
I just need your signature for these.

841
00:57:43,669 --> 00:57:45,504
<i>I'm going fishing today.</i>

842
00:58:23,334 --> 00:58:24,501
Attorney!

843
00:58:25,002 --> 00:58:26,086
Beth?

844
00:58:28,130 --> 00:58:29,965
Oh! Hi, Beth!

845
00:58:31,842 --> 00:58:33,260
You're here too.

846
00:58:35,596 --> 00:58:37,264
Remember that, Beth.

847
00:58:37,681 --> 00:58:38,933
Remember that.

848
00:58:55,157 --> 00:58:56,659
Problem solved.

849
00:58:57,409 --> 00:58:58,661
It's over.

850
00:59:00,663 --> 00:59:03,832
I hope that's enough to get Ana to stop.

851
00:59:14,927 --> 00:59:16,762
Don't tell me to stop!
You were kissing!

852
00:59:16,845 --> 00:59:17,972
- No!
You were kissing!

853
00:59:18,055 --> 00:59:19,056

How am I supposed to take that?

854
00:59:19,139 --> 00:59:21,225
- She kissed me!
It's the same thing!

855
00:59:21,308 --> 00:59:23,394
- Ana! Ana! Ana!
I saw you with her!

856
00:59:23,477 --> 00:59:25,145
Ben! Ben!

857
00:59:25,229 --> 00:59:26,981
- Ma'am! Ma'am, please leave!
Let me in! Miss!

858
00:59:27,064 --> 00:59:29,275
- I need to get inside!
Ma'am, you're not welcome!

859
00:59:29,358 --> 00:59:30,192
Ben!

860
00:59:30,276 --> 00:59:33,112
- Get me out of here!
Regina! What are you doing?

861
00:59:33,195 --> 00:59:35,030
- Imelda!
Get out of my way!

862
00:59:35,114 --> 00:59:36,782

I can't let them team up against Ana!

863
00:59:36,865 --> 00:59:40,494
<i>"Beth, I love you.</i>
<i>I'll leave my wife for you."</i>

864
00:59:40,577 --> 00:59:41,954
<i>Did you hear him say that?</i>

865
00:59:42,037 --> 00:59:43,163
He can't tell me,

866
00:59:43,247 --> 00:59:46,709
because his damn wife
is always hanging around!

867
00:59:46,792 --> 00:59:50,337
Which Bible says you have the right
to someone else's spouse?

868
00:59:50,421 --> 00:59:51,672


869
00:59:51,755 --> 00:59:53,382
Are you finally awake?

870
00:59:53,465 --> 00:59:56,260
You can reach all you want,

871
00:59:56,343 --> 00:59:59,096
but you will never, ever...

872
00:59:59,179 --> 01:00:00,306
touch what's mine.

873
01:00:00,389 --> 01:00:01,849
Okay. Okay.

874
01:00:01,932 --> 01:00:03,183
I'll take it instead.

875
01:00:03,267 --> 01:00:04,351
Come on.

876
01:00:04,435 --> 01:00:06,103
Better me than you.

877
01:00:08,355 --> 01:00:10,774

